1
00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:02,260
(Mrs Cooper:)Shelly! Dinner's ready!

2
00:00:02,260 --> 00:00:03,300
SHELDON: Coming!

3
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:04,560
(Mrs Cooper:)No cats!

4
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:05,980
(Penny:)Aw...

5
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,520
(Sheldon:)What is she doing here?

6
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:12,820
(Mrs Cooper:)I called her.

7
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:13,870
(Amy:)Your mother thinks

8
00:00:13,870 --> 00:00:15,820
(Amy:)you might be losing
your mind over me.

9
00:00:15,830 --> 00:00:18,480
(Amy:)As a neurobiologist, I was curious.

10
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:22,160
(Sheldon:)Well, rest assured, I am in
full possession of my faculties.

11
00:00:22,170 --> 00:00:25,280
(sneezes): 25 cats!

12
00:00:25,290 --> 00:00:28,590
(Mrs Cooper:)Oh, God bless you, dear.

13
00:00:28,590 --> 00:00:30,960
(Mrs Cooper:)Sheldon, sit down. Let's talk.

14
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:33,760
(Sheldon:)All right, but you're
not fooling me.

15
00:00:33,760 --> 00:00:34,980
(Sheldon:)Whenever you say we have to talk,

16
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,210
(Sheldon:)it means you want me to listen.

17
00:00:36,210 --> 00:00:37,210
(Mrs Cooper:)Then stop talking.

18
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:39,010
(Sheldon:)Yes, ma'am.

19
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:41,130
(Mrs Cooper:)Now, the reason I
called Amy over was

20
00:00:41,130 --> 00:00:43,690
(Mrs Cooper:)to find out what type
of person she is.

21
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:45,350
(Mrs Cooper:)And after chatting a bit,

22
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:47,690
(Mrs Cooper:)I have to say that while she is a

23
00:00:47,690 --> 00:00:51,190
perfectly unique young woman,

24
00:00:51,190 --> 00:00:54,710
(Mrs Cooper:)you two are definitely not
suited for each other.

25
00:00:54,710 --> 00:00:57,520
(Sheldon:)That's a peculiar conclusion.

